  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c001': '/* range-bar (range bar · form A "four-category swimlanes + row-end total + hour ticks"): start and end intervals placed on one axis,',
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c002': '   **length is "how long"**; the row-end total is the total duration of that category. When a segment is wide enough, the duration is written inside it again.',
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c003': "   Hierarchy comes not from shadows or large radii (receipt paper has zero shadow, big-type broadsheet zero radius): it comes from hairlines, font weight and shade steps ⇒ a reskin only swaps values. */",
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c004': "/* Head: title + purpose + total (the total hugs the right edge; when the container narrows, the three wrap on their own, none crushing another). */",
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c005': "/* **Tick row and swimlanes share the same column template** (`.ax` and `.lanes` are each a grid, the templates are identical word for word)",
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c006': "   ⇒ track width is identical, the tick ends always line up with the track ends. The two side columns are **fixed width** (wide tier 54 / 66, narrow tier 46 / 54):",
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c007': '   only fixed widths make "two grids with identical column widths" meaningful (`auto` would compute from each content and drift apart).',
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c008': "   The third track holds the total (duration / date), **wraps and never truncates**: longer wraps, never `…`. */",
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c009': "/* One swimlane = **three slots dropped straight into the grid above** (`display:contents`).",
