  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c011': "   If the tick row crowded in too (`grid-column:2` taking the first row’s second track), auto-placement would push the three slots of every swimlane",
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c012': '   into the wrong columns (the track would land in the first 46px column)—that is exactly what the criterion measuring "11px left overflow" caught in 2026-09. */',
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c013': "/* Ticks: always land in the track column; `flex-wrap` + column gap ⇒ however narrow it only wraps, never crushes text. */",
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c014': '/* Swimlane left column: mark + category name (the mark is the second path of "not by color alone", a long name wraps on its own). */',
  'base-render.components-range-bar-style.c015': "/* Swimlane right column: total (duration / date). The column is **fixed width**, so `overflow-wrap` wraps it **without truncation**",
