  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c002': "   the field row reads the current value, the selected row in the list shows the selected state; if the search finds nothing, create it right there without leaving to create it first. */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c003': "/* Field row: label + trigger key (the trigger key reads the current value). */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c004': "/* Floating surface: a top-layer surface, **anchored to the trigger key** (not to the viewport). Width = min(cap, viewport minus both side margins), long content scrolls inside.",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c005': "   Two-stage positioning (same as `popover-menu`): inside `@supports` it uses CSS anchor positioning (`position-area` against the trigger’s bottom edge,",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c006': "   flipping above when it does not fit), outside it falls back to a normal positioned element — `position: fixed; inset: auto` (**not** the UA",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c007': "   `inset: 0; margin: auto` centering: that would pin the surface to the viewport top edge, center it horizontally, and cover its own row),",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c008': "   and on open the runtime computes `left` / `top` from the trigger’s rectangle.",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c009': "   The inline block: the block that pushes open under the field row (single column, not side by side in the narrow tier). */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c010': "/* Anchor positioning (**only in engines that support the anchor API**): hugs the trigger’s left edge, the gap below = the `margin` above,",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c011': "   and if there is no room below it flips above the trigger. Both capability queries and the runtime **read the same constants** (`RELATION_PICKER_ANCHOR_QUERY` /",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c012': "   `RELATION_PICKER_AREA_QUERY`)—CSS and script must say the same thing about “does this engine support it”. */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c013': "/* The inline block and the row after selection (`style-forms.ts`): same discipline, same prefix, inserted here—",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c014': "   order is stacking order, the artifact is byte-identical before and after the change. */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c015': "/* Input row: the input spans the full width, the clear key is a fixed 44×44. */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c016': "/* Error state written next to the input (not color only): that is what `aria-describedby` points at. */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c017': "/* Column header row: the sources name on the left, the readout name on the right, same padding as every row below (readout length cannot squeeze the name). */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c018': "/* Column headers: each wraps inside its own segment (however long the readout, it cannot squeeze the name segment). */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c019': "/* Group title: only size / weight / letter-spacing and color, no fill and no rule (groups are separated by the 8px gap between rows). */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c020': "/* Row container, one option row and the matched term (`style-list.ts`): same discipline, same prefix, inserted here—",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c021': "   order is stacking order, the artifact is byte-identical before and after the change. */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c022': "/* Accessibility floor: a real keyboard user’s focus must be visible (focus is an **enhancement**, not the path—every row is tappable). */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c023': "/* Last row “create”: a leading sentence + the key that turns the current search term straight into a new entry (44 high, no line break). */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c024': "/* Empty state: appears when nothing matches (the footnote changes to “try a shorter term” at the same time). */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c025': "/* Footnote: what state this screen is in right now (frequent destinations / how many matched / try another term)—text swapped in place, no layout jump. */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c026': "/* The hint at the card bottom. */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c027': "/* Hover only enhances (and only on devices with a real pointer), tappability does not depend on it. */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c028': "/* Reduced motion: the press-step scale is switched off outright (nothing stuck halfway—states do not rely on transitionend). */",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c029': "/* Narrow tier (**the component itself** < {p0}px): **not one column folded**.",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c030': "   The list is single-column anyway; what the narrow tier really tightens is the inline left/right padding and those two seams: seam 10px→8px, padding drops 2px each,",
  'base-render.components-relation-picker-style.c031': "   giving that width to the name column (the inline block’s padding lives in `style-forms.ts`, same query). */",
